==================================================
LEVEL 12 - PURE PYTHON VS PANDAS

This is VERY important for interviews.

Take the SAME problem.

Solve it twice.

Example:

"Total revenue per customer."

Pure Python:

dictionary + loop

Then pandas:

groupby().sum()

Understand that these are not two different problems.

They are two implementations of the same operation.

This makes pandas much easier to learn.

==================================================
LEVEL 13 - LARGE DATASET THINKING

Learn the basic scalability questions.

Interviewer:

"What if the CSV is 10 GB?"

Think:

Do not load everything into memory.

Use streaming.

Pure Python:

for row in reader:
process(row)

Pandas:

Understand that normal read_csv loads substantial data into memory.

Know that chunking is possible:

pd.read_csv(
"large.csv",
chunksize=100000
)

Process each chunk.

You do NOT need distributed computing for this level.

